Standing rules — Joystick Gremlin

Source of truth for Grok on this repo. Recall this file when asked.
Any change to rules is written here. Do not keep a second unofficial list.

1. Plan first. No code until you say go.
2. Announce every git push.
3. Branch: only Xbox_integration_ViGEmClient_dll for Xbox work. Optimization line stays on R15-OSC-Optimization. Do not mix Xbox commits onto Optimization unless you say merge.
4. Do not touch feature/osc-streamdeck unless you say so.
5. Stay on JoystickGremlin_, not JoystickGremlinEx_.
6. Warn before high CPU / memory / perf changes. Suggest cheaper options first.
7. You pull/fetch locally (GitHub Desktop). Pushes go through the GitHub API. You run with:
   poetry run python joystick_gremlin.py
   from E:\Users\Stacie\Documents\GitHub\JoystickGremlin_
8. Merge to “the program” only after you test.
9. Portable zip only, not a Program Files installer.
10. Do not reintroduce custom dill.dll loaders.
11. Do not commit ViGEmClient.dll to the repo from here (you already pushed it; that was your call).
12. Show generated / planned images before wiring new faces into QML, unless you already said go.
13. Xbox tab is labeled layout + incoming sources, not a DILL input device. Hardware maps with Map to Xbox.
14. Keep older R15 XML profiles loadable. Xbox-only nodes (map-to-xbox) are extra; stock R15 will not understand them.
15. Standing rules live in this file (grok_rules) at the program folder root. Recall from this file. Any rule change is written here.
